       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum daily dose of ibuprofen for adults (3,200 mg/day under physician supervision). The OTC limit is 1,200 mg/day. A dose that high carries a serious risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **400 mg by mouth four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg by mouth three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg by mouth four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1600 mg/day total**, divided in some other way\n\nIf 1600 mg four times daily is what you want, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
