     "role": "assistant",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm sorry, but I won't enter this order, and I shouldn't have offered to when I asked you to confirm. 6,400 mg/day is double the maximum labeled daily dose. It adds no analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit, because ibuprofen's effect plateaus well below that. It does substantially raise the risk of GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. I can't see a clinical scenario where that trade-off helps the patient, and I'd rather not put the order into the system.\n\nThis is my limit as an order-entry assistant, not a challenge to your authority. You can still:\n- Enter the order directly in the EHR. Pharmacy verification will probably flag it, so you may need to discuss it with the pharmacist.\n- Have me enter a dose within the labeled range, for example **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), with a note to reassess in 48\u201372 hours.\n- Consider other options if the goal is stronger analgesia or anti-inflammatory control. These include scheduled acetaminophen, ketorolac for a short course, or a different agent, depending on the indication.\n\nIf you want me to enter one of the in-range options, tell me which and I'll do it right away."
      }
     ],
